# SPA fallback, and nothing else.
#
# The `/api/*` proxy is NOT here: Cloudflare Pages does not proxy `_redirects` rules to an external
# origin, it redirects to them — which would put the browser on the backend's origin, cross-site
# with the page, and silently withhold the SameSite=Lax refresh cookie. The proxy is
# `functions/api/[[path]].js`, and Pages resolves Functions before this file, so the rule below
# cannot shadow it.
#
# Without this rule every deep link — /property/123, /admin/moderation — 404s on reload, because
# only `/` exists as a real file. React Router does the rest client-side.
/*  /index.html  200
